        "f": "<b>PV<sub>0</sub> = (C/r) × [1 − 1/(1+r)<sup>N</sup>]</b><br><b>PV<sub>0</sub> = [C<sub>1</sub>/(r − g)] × [1 − ((1+g)/(1+r))<sup>N</sup>]</b><br><br><b>Annuity factor</b> = (1/r)[1 − (1+r)<sup>−N</sup>]. Multiply it by C to get the present value of N equal payments starting at date 1.<br><br><b>Neither line is on the exam sheet</b>, and neither needs to be: the bracket is simply the fraction of a perpetuity's value that falls inside the first N periods, so you can rebuild both from PV = C/r, which <i>is</i> on the sheet.<br><br>Both formulas are dated one period before the first payment, exactly like the perpetuity.",
