        "f": "<b>NWC<sub>t</sub> = w × Sales<sub>t</sub></b><br><b>ΔNWC<sub>t</sub> = w × (Sales<sub>t</sub> − Sales<sub>t−1</sub>)</b><br><br><b>Steady state.</b> If sales grow at a constant g, then ΔNWC<sub>t</sub> = g × NWC<sub>t−1</sub>, so a growing firm is <b>permanently</b> investing in working capital. Growth is not free, and a terminal year must carry this charge.<br><br><b>Note w can change.</b> If the problem alters the policy in one year (a new logistics system cutting inventory), the level jumps and ΔNWC for that year is a one-off <i>release</i> of cash. Never let that year set the terminal value.",
