        "s": "Write the CAPM and name every term. What is the security market line?",
        "f": "<b>r<sub>i</sub> = r<sub>f</sub> + β<sub>i</sub> × (E[R<sub>mkt</sub>] − r<sub>f</sub>)</b> &nbsp;(on the exam formula sheet)<br><br><b>r<sub>f</sub></b> — the risk-free rate, the reward for waiting.<br><b>(E[R<sub>mkt</sub>] − r<sub>f</sub>)</b> — the <b>market risk premium</b>, the reward per unit of beta.<br><b>β<sub>i</sub></b> — how many units of that risk the asset carries.<br><br><b>Security market line.</b> Plot required return against β: a straight line with intercept r<sub>f</sub>, slope equal to the market risk premium, passing through the market portfolio at β = 1. Every correctly priced asset sits on it, so the line reads both ways — beta in, return out, or return in, beta out.<br><br><b>Trap.</b> \"The market risk premium is 6%\" means E[R<sub>mkt</sub>] − r<sub>f</sub> = 6%. \"The expected return on the market is 6%\" with r<sub>f</sub> = 3% means the premium is only 3%. Underline which one you were given before writing anything, because the exam chains sub-questions and this error contaminates all of them.",
        "id": 10
