        "s": "Write the identity linking r_E, r_D and r_U, and state what this course calls the pre-tax WACC.",
        "f": "<b>r<sub>U</sub> = (E/V)·r<sub>E</sub> + (D/V)·r<sub>D</sub></b>, with V = E + D and <b>market values throughout</b>.<br><br>r<sub>U</sub> is the <b>unlevered cost of capital</b> — also called the asset cost of capital or the opportunity cost of capital: the return investors would demand if the firm carried no debt at all.<br><br><b>In this course the right-hand side is also the definition of the pre-tax WACC, so:</b><br><b>pre-tax WACC = r<sub>U</sub></b><br><br>Write that equality on your exam paper. It is a free consistency check on every leverage question you will ever be asked, and it is on the examiner's own list of checks.<br><br><b>Why it is not a theory but arithmetic:</b> if you own all the equity and all the debt, you own the assets, so your return must be the value-weighted average of the two.",
