        "s": "Write the beta weighting this course uses to unlever, and state what is deliberately absent from it.",
        "f": "<b>β<sub>U</sub> = [E/(E+D)]·β<sub>E</sub> + [D/(E+D)]·β<sub>D</sub></b><br><b>r<sub>U</sub> = r<sub>f</sub> + β<sub>U</sub>·(E[R<sub>mkt</sub>] − r<sub>f</sub>)</b><br><br>β<sub>U</sub> is the <b>unlevered beta</b> or <b>asset beta</b>: the systematic risk of the business itself.<br><br><b>What is absent: there is no (1 − τ<sub>c</sub>) on the debt weight.</b> Some textbooks weight debt by D(1 − τ<sub>c</sub>). FIE402 does not. This course assumes the firm rebalances to a target debt-to-value ratio, and under that assumption the tax shield carries the same risk as the assets, so it gets no separate treatment in the weighting.<br><br><b>Consequence of using the other version:</b> a different β<sub>U</sub>, a different r<sub>U</sub>, a different APV — and your WACC value will no longer equal your APV value. The examiner runs that check.",
