        "f": "The procedure for valuing a project or division whose own cost of capital you cannot observe. <b>Always in this order.</b><table class=\"data\"><tr><th>Rung</th><th>What you do</th><th>Formula</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Read the twin's cost of equity (or its share data)</td><td>r<sub>E</sub> given</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Back out the twin's equity beta</td><td>β<sub>E</sub> = (r<sub>E</sub> − r<sub>f</sub>)/(E[R<sub>mkt</sub>] − r<sub>f</sub>)</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Get the twin's debt beta, or 0 if the debt is stated risk-free</td><td>β<sub>D</sub> = (r<sub>D</sub> − r<sub>f</sub>)/(E[R<sub>mkt</sub>] − r<sub>f</sub>)</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><b>Unlever</b>, using the <i>twin's</i> weights</td><td>β<sub>U</sub> = (E/V)β<sub>E</sub> + (D/V)β<sub>D</sub></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Turn β<sub>U</sub> into a rate</td><td>r<sub>U</sub> = r<sub>f</sub> + β<sub>U</sub>(E[R<sub>mkt</sub>] − r<sub>f</sub>)</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><b>Relever</b> to <i>your</i> target D/E</td><td>β<sub>E</sub> = β<sub>U</sub> + (D/E)(β<sub>U</sub> − β<sub>D</sub>), then CAPM</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Build the WACC you need</td><td>pre-tax = r<sub>U</sub>; after-tax = (E/V)r<sub>E</sub> + (D/V)r<sub>D</sub>(1 − τ<sub>c</sub>)</td></tr></table><b>β<sub>U</sub> and r<sub>U</sub> are the only quantities that cross from the twin to you</b>, because they depend on the business and not on how it is financed. If a question appears to skip a rung, that rung's input was handed to you directly.<br><br>This routine has been tested in <b>all eleven mapped papers from 2015 to H2025</b>.",
